## 6. Storage Architecture

The initial storage architecture separates application infrastructure from user scan data.

EC2

Used for:

Operating system
MediVault application
Application-related local data

EC2 will use EBS for its block storage.

S3

Used for:

Medical scan images
Object-based application data

S3 will not have a customer-assigned IP address like an EC2 instance.

The application will access S3 through AWS APIs.

## 7. Security Goals

The infrastructure should follow these principles:

Least-privilege IAM permissions
S3 bucket should not be publicly accessible
S3 data should be encrypted
Administrative access should be restricted
Application access to S3 should use an IAM role rather than hard-coded credentials

## 8. Monitoring Goals

CloudWatch will be used to monitor:

EC2 health
EC2 resource utilization
S3 activity/metrics where applicable
Infrastructure health
